SOAPBOX: A fine time. Mostly. Parked up in the car, 1/4 wave whips, 100 W.
SOAPBOX: In BC we can get a good start on our Friday, as WPX begins at
SOAPBOX: 1700T (local.) Much fun to be had. A chance to get some before
SOAPBOX: the big hit of NA stns on NA Saturday, then tidy a bit on our
SOAPBOX: Sunday. Condx were fair. The fcsts appeared good, however
SOAPBOX: sometimes there was much noise, or not many folks. Day times
SOAPBOX: there was some amazing QSB on 10 and 15 m. The timing of the slow
SOAPBOX: fade/return was key for Low Power operating. I noticed a few more
SOAPBOX: stns using synth voice. It sometimes worked, other times not so
SOAPBOX: much. One of these used rather awkward "phonetics" for a letter
SOAPBOX: or two. A few stns were classic alligators, more power out, and
SOAPBOX: if poor RX was not down to local noise, then other inability to
SOAPBOX: hear stns. (Beyond just me!) Glad to get out, catch some familiar
SOAPBOX: call signs and voices. Was fun to work a handful of stns on
SOAPBOX: multiple bands. B1Z might be my first ever BY. I tried very hard
SOAPBOX: for Indonesia to no avail. Operating Classic I noticed those who
SOAPBOX: did not identify. A most interesting behaviour. I've op in M/M so
SOAPBOX: know how the flow may take one, however it's . . . useful to ID.
SOAPBOX: I tried rather uselessly to break the pile up for CY0S. Nice to hear
SOAPBOX: them from coast to coast though. 73 and tnx to all who worked me.
